<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech H1 C/A deficit rises to $1.7 bln (-$723 mln).</title>
<headline>Czech H1 C/A deficit rises to $1.7 bln (-$723 mln).</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Czech current account deficit for the first half of 1996 rose to $1.7 billion compared with a deficit of $723 million for the first half of 1995, the Czech National Bank said on Friday.</p>
<p>The capital posted a surplus for the first six months of $800.8 million compared with a surplus of $3.1 billion in the same period last year, the central bank added.  </p>
